WEBVTT

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.500
You are an embarrassment to gymnastics, damn it!

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.290
Huh? You are...

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.750
Minamino... Minamino... Minamino...?

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.080
No, Kitano!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.910
Idiot. He's Tetsuo Minamino.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.080
Well, what are you doing here?

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.290
No one told me you were coming.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.330
What is Nakanomori doi--

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:36.370
My coach has nothing to do with this.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.200
"Super Popular! Tama-chan on the Tama River"...

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.330
Not that!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.160
"Fake Retirement Samurai"...

00:00:53.910 --> 00:01:00.250
"Former Olympic medalist tricks the world
with a fake retirement press conference.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.500
What will the samurai who shakes up
the gymnastics world show us next?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.450
All eyes are on him."

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.500
Old man... I'll perform your last rites for you.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.330
Have a match with me.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.000
A match...?

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.750
--If you lose, then quit
gymnastics for sure this time--

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.370
--He'll accept that duel, indeed!
--If you lose, then quit
gymnastics for sure this time--

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:23.410
Good.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:24.580
Huh?

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.910
Who are you?

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.450
I'm Leo, indeed.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.540
Who are you?

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.160
A ninja, indeed.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.000
Who are you?

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.290
I said, I'm Leo, a ninja, indeed.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.700
D-Damn it...!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.790
Oh, you stay back.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.330
Very well.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:46.120
If you want a match, then we'll take you on.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.120
Huh?! We will?!

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.660
But we'll do it in a month and a half.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.910
He's injured right now, so he can't perform.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.500
Give me everything you've got.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.580
We're having a duel here, indeed!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:38.500
"The Gymnastics Samurai"

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.580
This is his performance
from last year's nationals.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.080
"Conviction"

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.080
Look at his layout Tkatchev.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:45.870
"Conviction"

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:52.200
He utilizes his wide and clean release
to confirm where he grabs on the bars.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.330
He's a gymnast with
outstanding aerial intuition.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.330
He lands multiple difficult moves
that are all close to perfection.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.540
He's a strong player who placed 5th
in the individual combined category.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.870
And he's still 17.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.750
He's undoubtedly the next ace gymnast.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.790
To tell you the truth,
since you're still rehabilitating,

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.750
it's unlikely that you would win.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.790
What? Then why did we accept the match?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:26.200
I figured you'd have your big
comeback at the next competition,

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.620
but you need to get back your
fighting intuition before then.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.410
That's just not possible in a practice setting.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.830
This is where that kid comes in.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.910
He's the perfect opponent for a serious match.

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.040
An unofficial match wouldn't
affect your records, either.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:45.120
It's a windfall, as they say.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:49.160
What? You're not up for it?

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:54.160
Knowing you... I thought you'd be all over it.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.790
Give me everything you've got.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.080
I'll do it.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.660
No, please allow me to do this.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.450
We'll start training tomorrow morning.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.450
Right!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.700
"Episode 3
'Dueling Samurai'"

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.830
"Episode 3
'Dueling Samurai'"
"Congratulations, Escaping Unemployment"

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.830
Congratulations for escaping unemployment!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.120
I'm so glad you were able
to make up with Mr. Amakusa!

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:22.580
You can bid farewell to your jobless days
once and for all, indeed!

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.450
Grandma was happy about it, too.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.160
What?

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.410
If you lose your job again, I'll kick you out.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.290
It's true!

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.910
But you know what?!
The good news doesn't end there.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:41.750
Huh?

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.290
Joe is about to challenge someone in a duel!

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.040
A duel...?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.500
Wow, with that gymnast who was on TV?

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.700
The "Bandana Prince," was it?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:56.410
So tell me, did he seem good?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.450
Yeah, he's strong.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:01.450
Joe's going to win because he's a samurai!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.290
Yeah! I'll do my best to help, too!

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.700
Rei...

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.410
Oh, yeah! Let's pray to God for help!

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.160
We'll pray to God for Joe's victory...

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.660
Huh?

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.660
Does it hurt?

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.040
A little.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.120
Seems like, other than your shoulder,
you're in good shape.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.750
The fatigue is totally gone.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.910
You should be able to resume
training without any issues now.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.370
Really?

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.700
But I won't let you overdo it.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.580
You'll obey my directions
no matter what. Got it?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.450
Yes.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.580
Good.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.160
I'll go over the training plan with you now.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.450
In brief, it's a body modification plan.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.000
Body modification?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.370
He's, without a doubt, a tough opponent.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.040
But it doesn't mean you don't stand a chance.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.750
Look. There's a slight gap between his legs.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.620
That's subject to a points deduction.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:10.200
Difficult techniques come with an
equal chance of earning or losing points.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.200
The same applies to you, too.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.500
Even if you execute a difficult technique,

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.500
it wouldn't be worth it
if you get points deducted.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.000
That's why we need to focus
on eliminating all errors.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.370
To make that happen...

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:30.370
...you need to have a sense
of stability with your body.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.580
Stability leads to precise technique.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.580
Your core, muscles...
We'll retrain every part of your body!

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.330
Give me one more set!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.410
Tighten your core!

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.290
Don't just rely on your strength.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.540
That's handstand basics, remember?

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:56.700
Yes!

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.410
Boom!

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.500
You seem like you're having a blast, Dad!

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.660
Oh, yeah? I'm actually exhausted from training.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.040
Really?

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.120
But you seem so spirited!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.870
How can I describe it...

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:21.160
It seems like you're able to do what you want!

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:25.870
Dad, you really are at your best
when you're doing gymnastics!

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:27.660
You think so?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.660
Yeah, it's true.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.540
Joe!

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.410
--You know I can help you
with stretching exercises!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.120
--Wait, wait, wait! Now's a really bad time! No!
--You know I can help you
with stretching exercises!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.410
--Wait, wait, wait! Now's a really bad time! No!
--Say, yo! Say, yo! Say, yo!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.500
--Do it! Do it!
--Say, yo! Say, yo! Say, yo!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.870
--Do it! Do it!
--Do it!

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.830
Leo, it's time for Sunday Western Theater!

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.410
Sunday... Wait, what?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.790
Huh?

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.250
Yeah!

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:36.540
--♪ Joe, Joe, Joe, Joe, indeed! ♪

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:38.700
--Samurai! Samurai! Samurai! Samurai!
--♪ Joe, Joe, Joe, Joe, indeed! ♪

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.290
--Samurai! Samurai! Samurai! Samurai!
--Oh? Is it a villain?

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:43.160
--Samurai! Samurai! Samurai! Samurai!
--Oh! Hey Rache--

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:48.000
--Samurai! Samurai! Samurai!
--Huh?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.080
Oh, hey, wait!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.450
Hmm...

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:55.950
So that's what happened.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:58.160
I see, poor Rei...

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:01.290
What do you think it was about?

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.540
That kinda thing...

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.080
...is totally Balkan Peninsula!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:07.950
Balkan... you say?

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.080
Did you get the supplies?

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.620
I'll be off right now!

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.330
What's up, Ayuchin?

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:17.950
What's with that lame outfit?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.540
Isn't it sick?! It's so sick!

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:22.250
The ninja look is in this year!

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.620
Ikebukuro will turn into Nikebukuro, just watch!

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.040
That's crazy.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.910
Right?! But anyway,
want to go grab dinner with me?

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.790
Can't you just eat here?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.870
What?

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:37.000
But wouldn't it be nice to go out sometimes?
I mean like us, alone...?

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.500
What do you want?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.290
Fried udon...?

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.040
The results are adequate.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.620
How's your pain level?

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:53.250
My pain level...

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.540
What...? It doesn't hurt at all...

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:03.120
You were dealing with chronic
inflammation in your shoulder joint.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:08.040
You won't feel pain as long as you train
the inner muscle that supports the joint.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.410
I wouldn't say you're fully recovered...

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.410
But for now, you can completely
focus on your performance.

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:15.750
Yes!

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.700
Huh?

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:19.080
We'll start practicing the moves now.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.330
I came up with the routine already.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.290
"Routine Plan" "1. Reverse Handstand"
"2. Giant Swing" "3. Layout Kovacs"
"4. Kovacs" "5. Piked Leg Stalder"

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.290
I didn't include the Aragaki this time.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.910
"6. Piked Stalder Single Turn" "7. Hop Half"
"8. Front Giant Swing" "9. Adler Turn"
"10. Triple Somersault"

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.910
I didn't include the Aragaki this time.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:32.500
You invented this triple
aerial flip technique...

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.790
It's known to be the hardest
flight move on the horizontal bar.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.160
But it's a great burden to your shoulders.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.950
Like I said, you're not fully recovered.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:44.500
I'm fully aware that the Aragaki
is a special move for you...

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.700
It's more than just a move you invented...

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.040
But I still can't let you do it...

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.750
As your coach.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:00.500
I've already entrusted you
with my gymnastics career.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:03.700
Good.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.000
"Future Aces
Introducing Athletes with Potential"

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.000
"Special Report: Gather 'round, Future Aces!"

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.500
"Future Aces
Introducing Athletes with Potential"

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.500
Lastly, we'll introduce

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.290
"Play Sports Club Athlete
Tetsuo Minamino (17)"

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:12.290
the young gymnast that's stirring up
the gymnastic world right now...

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.660
"Play Sports Club Athlete
Tetsuo Minamino (17)"

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.660
Tetsuo Minamino, also known
as the "Bandana Prince"!

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.790
Tetsuo Minamino, also known
as the "Bandana Prince"!

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.910
Hey, the duel is this Sunday, right?

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:20.910
Yeah.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.660
How's your condition?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.580
I feel pretty good!

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.290
I'll make lunch and go cheer for you!

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.620
Of course I'll come
running to join you, too!

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.660
Lady Mari, you're going, too, right?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:36.660
I'll pass. I've got the bar, too.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.120
All right.

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:39.250
How about you, BB?

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.120
What?!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.950
Um...

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.040
I'm a bird, you know?

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.200
You're still here?

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:56.700
I told you to finish up early
and prepare for tomorrow.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.830
Yes, I know... But...

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.000
What is it?

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.540
You nervous or something?

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.700
That's probably it...

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:06.950
Oh, come on.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:10.500
No... It just feels surreal.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:16.450
I faced defeat at the nationals
and was even set to retire once...

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:20.620
And yet... I'm here again.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:28.540
Tomorrow... I want to find out
how far I can go...

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.830
I just want to do my gymnastics!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.580
It's like a turtle's shell.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.160
Without it, you're not complete!

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:40.830
That's what gymnastics is to you.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.290
Amakusa...

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.410
I like turtles, too.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.040
Ah, you idiot...

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.540
I'm off.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.370
They're usually closed at this time...

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.830
But they agreed to let us use it
after I explained the situation.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.500
Looking forward to today.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:35.160
I'll be the judge. Any objections?

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.040
You'll go first, Jotaro.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.790
Jotaro! You've got this!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.160
Joe! Show him your samurai spirit!

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:47.910
Good luck, Dad!

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.290
"Samurai"

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.290
Good luck, Dad!

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.290
Yeah.

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:58.700
Ready?

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.870
Yes!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:20.620
So high!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:23.910
That's Jotaro's horizontal bar for you.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.080
He won his medals with that height.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.120
The layout Kovacs!

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.830
That's the Kovacs!

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:40.200
Idiot, you're too far!

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:44.160
Shoot, I'm too far. Can I grab it?

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.120
No, I <i>will </i>grab it!

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:54.080
I've got this. I can do this!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.660
All right! Perfect landing!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:28.830
Yes!

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.910
That was crazy, Jotaro!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:32.830
That was unbelievable!

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:35.370
That was brilliant, Joe!

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:39.700
That was amazing! It was really amazing, Dad!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.790
What fools...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.000
Move.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.500
Wonder what he's got.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.120
Yeah...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:10.000
A perfect layout Kovacs.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.370
He's improved since the nationals.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.700
Wow...

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:32.910
A triple flip?!

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:35.120
Isn't that Dad's...?

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:37.370
Ara... gaki...

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:54.500
Do you get it now?

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:57.750
There's no place for you in gymnastics anymore.

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:03.000
Vanish. Don't ever come back.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:06.040
Dad... Did you lose?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.370
What a guy...

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:14.580
It's unbelievable how he
perfected his techniques.

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.620
And that Aragaki...

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:20.250
He's mastered it in such a short time...

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.200
Then...

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:28.790
This means I can still do this!

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.370
Thanks to you, I can see my next goal!

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.370
Thanks!

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.200
Get away!

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:39.120
I told you to quit gymnastics if you lose!

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.000
To quit...?

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.200
You're gonna play dumb now?!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:51.250
Ninja Art: Dogeza!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.620
What?!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:53.540
What the heck are you--

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.160
I beg you, please!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:58.580
Please let Joe continue on with gymnastics!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:02.580
He may have lost the duel,
but his performance was fantastic!

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.000
It gave me the chills, watching him!

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.620
That's Joe's... the Samurai's gymnastics!

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.700
I'd love to see more!

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.370
So I beg you!

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.830
Please don't take away gymnastics from Joe!

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:19.870
You...

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:22.330
I ask for the same thing.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.580
Amakusa?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.500
He should be able to give an even better
performance at the next competition.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:31.830
It'll silence those who accuse
him of retirement fraud.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:35.080
So... please...

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.950
I beg you, indeed!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.290
This is ridiculous.

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.080
What...

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:06.870
We'll meet again... at the competition!

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:20.950
Jotaro, the competition's in the spring.
There's no time to relax.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:23.450
I'm going to be stricter than ever...

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.450
So brace yourself.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.450
Yes!

00:23:00.790 --> 00:23:02.700
You bastard, that was a fixed race!

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:06.790
Get outta here! Can't pull off
a fixed race like that.

00:23:06.790 --> 00:23:07.870
Huh?
